BC-250 amdgpu kernel patch series
================================

patches/0001-0006
-----------------
Source:  https://github.com/MastaG/linux-cachyos-bc250
Commit:  f05991ace64a42eda3d2dc583e96b8d35ce393e3
License: GPL-2.0-only (LICENSE)

  0001  GFX1013 PASID TLB invalidation
        The KIQ-routed PASID TLB invalidation corrupts sustained KFD
        workloads on this die. Route GFX1013 through MMIO instead.
        Original work: the compute-queue research in
        https://github.com/DryhoppedIPA/bc250-gfx1013-fix

  0002  GFX1013 compute gfxoff guard
        amdgpu_gfx_off_ctrl() is not reached for GFX1013 by the generic
        gfx10 path, so compute-idle transitions leave the GPU in a state
        the compute queue does not survive. Drive it explicitly.

  0003  BC-250 KFD TLB flush by runlist
        The HWS path on this chip does not expose a usable PASID to VMID
        mapping to the normal gfx10 TLB flush. Rebuild the active runlist
        instead, which is the invalidation path measured to work here.

  0004  amdgpu TTM NULL page guard
        Partial TTM population can leave NULL entries in the page vector.
        Four lines that turn a NULL dereference into a no-op.

  0005  Cyan Skillfish sclk range
        The kernel-side clamp was 1000-2000 MHz; the part runs 350-2230.
        Widening it lets the governor reach the 40CU sweet spot and lets
        the card idle lower.

  0006  BC-250 40CU unlock
        From duggasco (https://github.com/duggasco/bc250-40cu-unlock).
        Writes CC_GC_SHADER_ARRAY_CONFIG, SPI_PG_ENABLE_STATIC_WGP_MASK and
        RLC_PG_ALWAYS_ON_WGP_MASK during CU enumeration. Off by default:
        amdgpu.bc250_cc_write_mode defaults to 0 and every write is guarded
        on PCI device id 0x13FE.

patches/0007
------------
Source:  https://github.com/Thunkar/bc250-bazzite-toolkit
Commit:  f2b3d7687af848744084a355a01be3d28e0dce75
License: GPL-2.0-only (LICENSE). The upstream file is MIT; it is a kernel
patch and is carried as GPL-2.0.

  0007  Read-only bc250_gfx1013 marker parameter
        Lets userspace tell a patched amdgpu from the stock one. The
        upstream description called the series "compute-queue lifecycle"
        patches; that description is corrected here.

Not carried
-----------
The 8-core telemetry series (MastaG 0001-0004) is not included. It only
matters on a board with the SMU firmware patched for eight cores, which
this image does not support, and it rewrites the SMU metrics interfaces.

The display patches (DCN201 and CH7218, MastaG 0012-0017 and 0020) are not
included. They are specific to DP to HDMI 2.1 active adapters and to the
governor's forced clock commits, and they need board-specific validation
before they belong in a general image.

The deferred-OD-commit series (MastaG's disabled/ directory) is not
included. It is the documented fix for a governor commit racing HDMI FRL
link training, and it is worth reading before adopting; it is not a change
to ship blind.
